---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../site';

const steps = [
  {
    step: 'Start here',
    title: 'What is PH?',
    text: 'What pulmonary hypertension is, how it affects your body, and the five types.',
    href: '/what-is-ph/',
  },
  {
    step: 'Step 2',
    title: 'Diagnosis and tests',
    text: 'The usual path from GP to diagnosis, and the tests you might have along the way.',
    href: '/diagnosis-and-tests/',
  },
  {
    step: 'Step 3',
    title: 'Questions for your doctor',
    text: 'A printable list to take to your next appointment.',
    href: '/questions-for-your-doctor/',
  },
  {
    step: 'Step 4',
    title: 'Treatments',
    text: 'The main types of PH medicines, supportive treatments and surgery.',
    href: '/treatments/',
  },
  {
    step: 'Step 5',
    title: 'Find a specialist',
    text: 'Hospitals in Australia and New Zealand with PH services.',
    href: '/find-a-specialist/',
  },
];
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Navigating life with pulmonary hypertension, <em>together</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Plain-language information for people with pulmonary hypertension (PH) and their families in Australia and New
      Zealand.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="review-box" role="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Early preview.</strong> The health information here has not yet been clinically reviewed. Always check
      with your doctor or PH specialist team. <a href={url('/about/')}>About this site</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="journey-heading">
    <h2 id="journey-heading">Recently diagnosed? Start here</h2>
    <ul class="path-grid">
      {steps.map((s) => (
        <li>
          <a class="path-card" href={url(s.href)}>
            <span class="step">{s.step}</span>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="prose" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
    <h2 id="what-heading">PH in brief</h2>
    <p>
      Pulmonary hypertension is high blood pressure in the lungs. It is a rare, complex condition that affects the
      arteries in the lungs and the right side of the heart.
    </p>
    <p>
      Unlike regular high blood pressure, it can't be measured with a cuff on your arm. Because the right side of the
      heart has to work harder to pump blood through narrowed lung arteries, people with PH often have breathlessness,
      tiredness and chest pain.
    </p>
    <p>
      PH is a serious condition and there is currently no cure for most types. Treatments have improved a lot, and
      with specialist care many people live well for years after diagnosis.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
